From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] add the vendored libraries' licence text

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [licence text for dependencies fetched at build time, not part of the upstream sdist]

The wheel's CIBW_BEFORE_ALL_LINUX step builds libgc.so (Boehm-Demers-Weiser
garbage collector 8.2.12, github.com/ivmai/bdwgc) and libhomfly.so
(libhomfly 1.04, github.com/miguelmarco/libhomfly) from their pinned,
sha256-verified upstream release tarballs, and auditwheel vendors both
into the wheel, but those tarballs are fetched at build time and never
land in the sdist, so nothing carries their licence text.

libhomfly's own tarball ships a LICENSE file (the Unlicense / public
domain dedication); gc's README.md carries a permissive copyright-and-
licence notice instead of a separate file. Dropping both at the package
root as LICENSE.libhomfly and LICENSE.gc lands them in dist-info/licenses/
via the same PEP 639 default glob as the package's own LICENSE (gotcha 53).

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/pkgs/sagemath-homfly/LICENSE.gc b/pkgs/sagemath-homfly/LICENSE.gc
new file mode 100644
